hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8676","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Hisham bin Malas Al-Nimri told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Al-Assam, Yazid bin Al-Assam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The The One who possessed the images, ever since he was appointed to do so, looked towards the throne for fear of being ordered to, before his eyes returned to him, as if his eyes were two stars. Duryan: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8676 - Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions"
"8677","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi informed me, and Mutarrif bin Tarif Al-Harithi told us, on the authority of Atiya bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in his saying God Almighty: {And when the trumpet is blown} [Al-Mu’minun: 101], the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How can He be blessed when the owner of the trumpet has reached the top of the horn, and is bent? He placed his forehead and listened with his hearing, waiting for when he would be commanded. The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How should we say, O Messenger of God? He said: “Say, ‘Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs in Allah. We put our trust.’” The focus of this hadith is on the authority of Abu Sa’eed, may God be pleased with him.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8677 - Attiya is weak"
"8678","Abu Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Ismail Abu Yahya Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How can he be blessed when the owner of the century has embraced the century, and he has bowed his forehead and listened with his ears, waiting? When is it commanded that it be blown? We said: O Messenger of God, so how should we say? He said: “Say, ‘Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs. We put our trust in Allah.’” We did not write it from the hadith of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id except With this chain of narration, had Abu Yahya al-Taymi not been on the road, I would have deemed the hadith to be authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them. This hadith has its origin in the hadith of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8678 - Abu Yahya Wah"
"8679","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Amr bin Al-Nadr bin Amr Al-Harashi told us, and Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us: We told him: Yahya bin Yahya reported on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no morning without two angels calling, one of them says: O God, give a successor to a spender, and the other says: O God. Give a catcher that is destroyed, and two angels appointed with images await when they are commanded and they will blow, and two angels call out, one of them saying: Woe to the men who Women, and the other says: Woe to women from men. “It was only narrated by Kharijah bin Musab, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8679 - Kharijah is weak"
"8680","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, and Bishr Ibn Al-Fadl, they said: Suleiman Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Ijli, on the authority of Bishr Ibn Shaghaf, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with him. It was narrated from them that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the pictures. He said: “A horn that is blown into.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8680 - True"
"8681","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, in Kufa, Hussein bin Ali told us. Al-Jufi’i, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Abi Aws, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, one of the best of your days is Friday. On it, Adam was created, on it he died, on it the trumpet is blown, and on it is the thunderbolt. So pray for me a lot during it, for your prayers have been presented to me. They said: How will our blessings be presented to you since you have died? He said: “God Almighty has forbidden the earth to eat the bodies of the prophets.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8681 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8682","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told me, about Ya`la ibn Ata’, on the authority of Waki` ibn Adas, on the authority of his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqaili, may God be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of God, did we eat it? His Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and what is the sign of that in His creation? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Aren’t all of you looking at the moon when it is empty?” They said: Yes, he said: “God is greatest.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, how does God bring the dead to life, and what is the sign of that in His creation? He said: “Did you not pass through your family’s valley?” He said: Yes, he said: “Then you passed by it and it was turning green?” He said: Yes, he said: “Thus does God give life to the dead, and that is His sign in His creation.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8682 - True"
"8683","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Yaqoub bin Issa told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Mugheerah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ayyash, on the authority of Dulham bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hajib bin Amer, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle Laqit ibn Amir said that he went out to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with him was Nahik ibn Asim ibn Malik ibn al-Muntafiq. He said: So we came Medina at the end of Rajab, so we prayed the morning prayer with him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and addressed the people, and said: “O people, I I have hidden my voice for you for four days so that I can hear you. Is there a person sent by his people? They said: Know for us what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says. Then perhaps he will be distracted by his own conversation, or by the conversation of his companion, or distracted by it. Misguidance. Indeed, I am responsible. Have I conveyed the message? O listen and you will live. O listen and you will live. Sit down. So the people sat down, and I and my companion stood up until, when His heart and sight were empty for us. I said: O Messenger of God, I am asking you about my need, so do not rush me. He said: “Ask whatever you want.” I said: O Messenger By God, do you have any knowledge of the unseen? He laughed at Omar Allah, shook his head, and knew that I sought his downfall.He said: “Your Lord has conceived five keys from the unseen, and no one knows them except God.” And he gestured with his hand, and I said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “He knew when one of you would die and you did not know it, and He knew when rain would come over you, looking down and out of pity.” So he continued to laugh and he continued to laugh. He knew that your relief was near.” A foundling said: I said: O Messenger of God, we will never be without a Lord who will laugh with goodness. “And He knew what lies ahead, and He knew what you would be obedient to.” tomorrow and you do not know it, but he knows the Day of the Hour.” He said: “And I think it is a mention of what is in the wombs.”\nHe said: So we said: O Messenger of God, we know from what the people know, and what you know, we are from a tribe who do not believe our truth from Madhhij, which is over upon us, and Khath’am who are our allies, and our clan from which we are. He said: “You will remain for as long as you remained, then your Prophet will die, and then you will remain for as long as You remained for a while, then the cry would be raised. For the life of your God, you will not leave anything on the face of the earth without it dying, and so are the angels who are with your Lord, so the earth emptied. Then your Lord sent the heavens to clear up from under the throne, so for the life of your God you will not leave on its back the death of a slain person or the burial place of a dead person unless it is torn apart. The grave is removed from him until he creates it from the front of his head and he is sitting level, your Lord will say: Mighty? So he says: Oh Lord, yesterday,Because of his covenant with life, he considers it a conversation with his family. “So I said: O Messenger of God, how can he bring us together after the winds, the calamities, and the wild beasts have torn us apart? He said: “I inform you of a similar thing about God’s blessings. The earth looked upon it as a ruined ruin, and I said, ‘It will never live again.’ Then your Lord sent the heaven upon it.” She did not wait for a few days until she looked at it, and behold, it was one drink, and the life of your God is more powerful than water to gather you together. On the condition that He gathers the plants of the earth, and you emerge from the branches of your farms, and you look at Him for an hour, and He looks at you.” He said: I said: Oh Messenger of God, how come he is one person and we the entire earth look at him and he looks at us? He said: “I inform you of something like that regarding the signs of God, the sun and the moon. A sign from Him is close and small. You will see them in one hour, and He will see you without “You are guaranteed to see them, and because your God is willing to see you and you see him, he is more capable than they are to see you and you see them.”\nI said: O Messenger of God, what will our Lord do to us when we meet Him? He said: “You will present to Him your pages as a plain to Him, and nothing of you will be hidden from Him. Then your Lord will take with His hand a scoop of water and sprinkle it with it.” Before you, for the life of your God, not a drop will miss the face of any of you.As for the believer, you cover his face like a white bandage, and as for the disbeliever, you cover his face with black lava, then your Prophet departs. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the righteous will pass in his wake - or he said: the righteous will depart in his wake - “He said: “So they will walk on a bridge of fire on which none of you will tread. Jamarat, and he says: Feel it, and your Lord says - or He said: Then they will look at the Messenger’s basin on a thirsty, by God, exhausting body that I have never seen before. By the life of your God, not one of you spreads his hand - or he said: none of you drops - a cup that purifies it from filth, urine, and impurity. And the sun and the moon will be saved - or he said: The sun and the moon will be withheld - so you will not see one of them.” So I said: O Messenger of God, what will we see on that day? He said: “Like the sight of your hour, on a day when the earth opened and the mountains faced.”\nI said: O Messenger of God, how will we be rewarded for our bad deeds and our good deeds? He said: “A good deed will be rewarded ten times the same, and a bad deed will be rewarded the same, or it will be forgiven.”\nI said: O Messenger of God, what is Paradise and what is Hell? He said: “By the life of your God, Paradise has eight gates, of which there are only two gates, and between them is a rider’s journey of seventy years.And indeed, Hell has seven gates, of which there are only two gates, and between them is the journey of a rider of seventy years.” I said: O Messenger of God, what will come from Heaven? He said: “Rivers of pure honey, rivers of milk whose taste has not changed, and rivers of a cup that has no headache or regret, and who Water that is not stagnant, and with fruit for the life of your God. You do not know anything better than the like of it, with purified pairs with it.” I said: O Messenger of God, give us priority in it. Reconciling husbands? He said: “Good deeds are for the righteous. You will find pleasure in this world as much as you enjoy, and they will enjoy you unless you do not reproduce.” I said: O Messenger of God. Is this the utmost we can reach?\nThen I said: O Messenger of God, for what do I pledge allegiance to you? He said: So he extended his hand and said: “To establish prayer and pay zakat, and beware of polytheism. Do not associate anything with God - or associate with God anyone but Him.” I said: And indeed, between the East and the West is ours. He clenched his fists and extended his fingers and thought that I was stipulating something that he would not give me. So I said: We will solve it. From it wherever we want, and no one commits any harm except against himself? He said: “That is yours. Take part of it wherever you wish, and do not blame anyone but yourself.” So we pledged allegiance to him and then we left.He said: “Indeed, these two, by the age of your god, are among the most truthful and God-fearing of people at first and last.” Ka’b bin Fulan, one of the sons of Bakr bin, said: Dogs: Who are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “Banu al-Muntafiq,” so I approached him and said: O Messenger of God, is there any good among us who passed away during the pre-Islamic era? Then a man from the vicinity of Quraysh said: Your father is the one who is in hellfire. It is as if he fell free between my skin, face and flesh, from what he said to my father in front of the people. So I thought to say: And your father, O Messenger of God, then I looked and saw the other one was more beautiful, so I said: And your family, O Messenger of God? He said: “And my family, for the sake of God, whatever grave you come to from the grave of a Quraysh or an Amirite polytheist, say: Muhammad has sent me to you, so give me good news of what will harm you, and you will be rewarded.” On your face and your stomach in the Fire.” So I said: Why should I do this to them, O Messenger of God? And they were in a position that they thought they had no religion except Him. And they thought they were reformers? He said: “This is because God sent a prophet to the last of every seven nations. So whoever obeys his prophet is among the guided, and whoever disobeys his prophet is among those who are lost.” This is a comprehensive hadith on this topic with an authentic chain of narration. They are all Medinans and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8683 - Yaqoub bin Muhammad bin Isa Al-Zuhri is weak"
"8684","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah told us, Baqiyya told us, Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “On the Day of Resurrection, people will be raised barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” She said: Aisha: O Messenger of God, what about the private parts? He said: “Every one of them on that day will have a matter that will enrich him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not mention it with this addition. The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadiths of Amr bin Dinar and Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, with its length Without mentioning the faults therein.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8684 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8685","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Al-Walid told me Ibn Juma’ al-Qurashi, Abu al-Tufayl Aamir ibn Wathilah narrated to me, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Asid, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: He narrated to me The truthful, the trustworthy, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The people will be gathered in three groups: one group feeding, clothed and riding, and another group walking and running. And in droves the angels will drag them on their faces to the Fire. Then we said: O Abu Dharr, we have known these and those, so what is the matter with those who walk? And they strive? He said: “Allah casts a calamity on the back, but it does not come back.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration from Al-Walid ibn Juma’, but they did not narrate it."
"8686","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Jamal told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, and Ali Bin Asim, they said: Bahz bin Hakim bin Muawiyah told us, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub, the memorizer, and the pronunciation of it, told us. Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Bahz bin Hakim bin Muawiyah speaking, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, where do you command me? Come down to me, he said: Then he waved his hand towards the Levant, and said: “You are gathered, foot and mounted, and you are being dragged on your faces here.” And he waved with his hand. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Abu Qaza Suwayd bin Hujayr, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, similar to the narration of Bahz, with the fact that Bahz is also safe and does not need to be narrated. His narration to a follower\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8686 - True"
"8687","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Hakim Bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “You will be gathered here barefoot and naked, walking and riding. And on your faces you will be exposed to God, and on your mouths will be sacrifice, and the first thing that will be expressed by one of you is his thigh.”"
"8688","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Saad, who said: We were sitting with Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, and he recited: {On the Day of We will gather the righteous to the Most Gracious as a delegation.} [Maryam: 85] He said: “No, by God, they will not be gathered on their feet, nor will they be led as a driver, but rather they will be brought with camels. From the dawn of Paradise, creation has never seen the like of it. Their mounts are gold and their edges are emeralds, so they sit on it until they knock on the door of Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8688 - It is not correct"
"8689","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Saeed bin Abu Hilal told him that he heard Othman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Qurazi say: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, read the words of God Almighty: {And indeed you have come to Us singly, just as We created you the first time} [Al-An'am: 94] Then she said: O Messenger of God, and the worst of it is that men and women will be gathered together. Do they look at each other? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every one of them on that day will have a business that will enrich him. The men will not look at the women, nor will the women look at them.” “Men, some of them were distracted from one another.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8689 - There is a break"
"8690","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukair told us, Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The last to be gathered are two shepherds from Muzainah. They go to Medina, crowing at their sheep, and find them to be wild beasts. They reached Thaniyat al-Wada` and fell on their faces. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8690 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8691","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ishaq bin Yahya told us Ibn Talha Ibn Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ma’bad Ibn Khalid, said: I entered the mosque and suddenly an old man was walking around, so I greeted him and he returned my greetings. I sat next to him and said: Who are you, uncle? He said: Rather, who are you, my nephew? I said: I am Ma`bad bin Khalid. He said: Welcome. I know your father. He was with me in Damascus, and your father and I were the first two knights to stand at the gate. A virgin - a city in the Levant - so I said: Who are you? He said: I am Abu Sariha al-Ghifari, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: He told me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Yes, I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Two men will be gathered from Muzainah. They will be the last people to be gathered. They will come from a mountain that they have climbed until They go to the places of the people and find the land and monsters until they come to the city. When they reach the nearest part of the city, they say: Where are the people? They did not see anyone, and one of them said: The people are in their houses. So they entered the houses and, lo, there was no one in them, and lo and behold, there were foxes and cats on the mattresses. They say: Where are the people? So one of them says: The people are in the mosque. They go to the mosque and do not find anyone. They say: Where are the people? Then one of them says: The people in the market are occupied by the markets, so they go out until they come to the markets, but they do not find anyone there, so they set off until They come to the second place and, lo, there are two angels over it. They seize them by their feet and drag them to the land of the gathering. They will be the last of the people to be gathered. “This is An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8691 - Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha said: Ahmad Matruk"
"8692","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Muammar narrated, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the verse was revealed: “O people, fear your Lord. The earthquake of the Hour is a great thing} [Al-Hajj: 1] upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was on his way, so he raised his voice with it until his companions responded to him. He said: “Do you know what day this is?” On the Day when God will say to Adam: “O Adam, arise and send forth a messenger of the Fire from every thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine.” So that was difficult for the Muslims. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Strike, approach, and give good tidings. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are among the nations nothing but like a mole on the side of A camel, or like a lump in the arm of an animal, for there are with you two creations that were not with anything except that you multiplied them, Gog and Magog, and whoever is destroyed is \"This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\""
"8693","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Dawrqi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, so he committed sin. The hadith is similar to it, then Muhammad bin Yahya said at the end of it: “This hadith according to us is not preserved from Anas, but what is preserved with us is The hadith of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn,"
"8694","Abd al-Samad narrated it to us, Hisham narrated it to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of al-Hasan. The imam of the imams, Muhammad bin Yahya al-Dahli, may God be pleased with him, ruled On his authority, Muhammad bin Ismail and Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj, may God be pleased with them, did not include a word in this translation, and they mentioned that Al-Hasan did not He hears from Imran bin Husayn. Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “What I have is that Al-Hasan heard from Imran bin Husayn.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8692 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8695","The hadith was narrated to us by Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Abu Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Al-Minhal Al-Dair narrated to us, they said: Muadh narrated to us. Ibn Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said the salutation on his way, and his companions’ journey had varied, so he raised his voice with these two verses: “O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is something.” Great} [Al-Hajj: 1] Abu Musa read up to his saying: {But the punishment of God is severe} [Al-Hajj: 2] When his companions heard that, they urged the mount, and they knew that he When he said something, he said: “Do you know what day that is?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “That is the day when Adam will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: O Adam, send forth a messenger of the Fire from every thousand. “Nine hundred and ninety-nine in Hell and one in Paradise.” So his companions became foolish, to the point where they explained with a laugh. When the Messenger of God saw May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his Companions. He said: “Work and give good tidings. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creatures who were not with anything except You have multiplied it, Gog and Magog, and whoever is destroyed from the children of Adam and the children of Satan.” So some of what they found was hidden from the people, then he said: “Work And give good tidings, for by the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, you are not among the people but like a mole on the side of a camel, or like a spot on the arm of an animal,” and so on. Narrated by Saeed bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada"
"8696","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdan Al-Saadi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Saeed bin Abi told us Orouba, and Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him He said hello in some of his travels, so he mentioned the hadith similarly, and we have narrated this hadith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas."
"8697","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Suleiman told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, about Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse And with his companions: {O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a great thing} [Al-Hajj: 1] until the end of the verse, so he said: “Do you know what That day? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “That is the day when God will say to Adam: Arise and be sent to the Fire - or he said: sent to the Fire - and he will say: O Lord. From how much? He said: “Out of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine will go to Hell, and one will go to Paradise.” So that was distressing to the people, and distress fell upon them. And sadness. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I hope that you will be half the people of Paradise.” They rejoiced, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Work and give good tidings, for you are between two creations. They were not with anyone except that You multiplied them, Gog and Magog. You are only among the people - or among the nations - Like a mole on the side of a camel or like a spot on the arm of a camel, but my nation is only one part of a thousand.” This is an authentic hadith with this addition. And they did not take him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8697 - True"
"8698","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan told us, and Muhammad bin Kathir told us, they said: Mahdi bin Maymun, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Bishr bin Shaghaf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, who said: We were sitting in the mosque. On Friday, he said: “The greatest day of the world is Friday. On it Adam was created and on it the Hour will come. And the most honorable of God’s creation is God’s father.” Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I said: May God have mercy on you, so where are the angels? He said: He looked at me and laughed and said: “O my nephew, do you know what angels are?” The angels are only a creation like the creation of the heavens and the earth and the winds and the clouds and the rest of creation that does not disobey God at all, and that Paradise is in the heavens. Fire in the earth. When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will resurrect the creation, nation by nation, and prophet by prophet, until Ahmad and his nation will be the last of the nations to be stationed. He said: Then he will rise, and his nation, whether righteous or immoral, will follow him. Then the bridge of Hell will be placed, and they will take the bridge, and God will blur the eyes of his enemies. They will rush into it from the left and the right, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the righteous with him will be saved, and the angels will meet them and show them their homes of Paradise is on your right, on your left, until he reaches his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, and a throne is placed for him on the right of God, the Mighty and Majestic. Then a herald calls: Where is Jesus? And his nation? Then he will rise, and his nation, both righteous and immoral, will follow him. They will take the bridge, and God will blur the sight of His enemies, and they will rush into it from the north. And to the right, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the righteous with him will be saved, and the angels will meet them and show them their homes in Paradise on your right hand. He will walk to his left until he reaches his Lord and a throne is placed for him from the other side. He said: Then the prophets and nations will follow them until there is The last of them was Noah, may God have mercy on Noah. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it and it is not fabricated, for Abdullah bin Salam was the first to know An ancient narration from among the Companions, and he attributed it by mentioning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in more than one place, and God knows best.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8698 - True"
"8699","Abu Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Al-Walid Al-Fahham told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he recited: {The day the sky will split open with the clouds, and the angels descended in a descent} [Al-Furqan: 25] He said: “The heaven of the world will split open and the angels will descend upon every heaven, and the people of the lowest heaven, and they are more numerous than those on earth, both jinn and humans, so the people of the earth say: Is our Lord among you? They say: No, then the people of the second heaven come down and they are more than the people of the lowest heaven and the people of the earth, and they say: Is our Lord among you? They say: No, then the people of the third heaven descend, and they are more than the people of the second heaven, the heavens of this world, and the people of the earth, and they say: Is our Lord among you? They say: No, then the people of the fourth heaven descend, and they are more than the people of the third and second heaven, the world, and the people of the earth. They say: Is our Lord among you? They say: No, then the people of the fifth heaven descend, and they are more than the people of the fourth, third, and second heavens, and the world, and the people of The earth, and they say: Is our Lord among you? And they say: No,Then the people of the sixth heaven will descend, and they are more than the people of the fifth, fourth, third, and second heavens, and the world, and the people of The earth, and they say: Is our Lord among you? They say: No, then the people of the seventh heaven descend and they are more than the people of the sixth, fifth, fourth and third heavens. And the second: And the world and the people of the earth say: Is our Lord among you? And they say: No. Then the cherubim will descend, and they are more numerous than the inhabitants of the seven heavens and the two earths, and those who bear the throne will have horns, ankles like ankles. The distance between someone's feet is such-and-such, and from the sole of his foot to his heel is a journey of five hundred years, and from his heel to his knee. The journey of five hundred years, and from his knee to the socket the journey of five hundred years, and from his collarbone to the place of the earring the journey of five hundred years. General: “The narrators of this hadith on the authority of the last of them are cited as evidence other than Ali bin Zayd bin Jad’an al-Qurashi, although he is based on Ibn Abbas.” It is quite strange.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8699 - Its chain of transmission is strong\n Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Aba Ishaq, saying: I heard Hubayra bin Yarim, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud,May God be pleased with him, he recited {The day the earth will be changed into another earth} [Ibrahim: 48]. He said: “A land like silver, white and pure, on which no blood has been shed and no work has been done.” In it is a sin. The caller will hear them and the sight will take them away, barefoot and naked standing, then sweat will cover them.” It was said on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymoon, on the authority of Abdullah\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8699 - Its chain of transmission is strong"
"8700","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, On the authority of Abu Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun, speaking, on the authority of Abdullah, in His saying, the Almighty, the Most High: {The Day when An earth other than the earth and the heavens.} [Ibrahim: 48] He said: “A white and pure land on which no blood has been shed and no sin has been committed. The caller will hear them. “And their sight will leave them barefoot and naked, as they were created, until the sweat covers them.” This hadith is authentic with all its chains of narration, on the condition of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8700 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8701","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddy told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza Al-Zubairi told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The earth will be extended with a tide on the Day of Resurrection. Due to the greatness of the Most Gracious, then no human being from the children of Adam will have anything but a place for his feet. Then the first of people will be called and he will prostrate himself, then permission will be given to me and I will stand up. So I say: O Lord, this told me - to Gabriel while he is on the right of the Most Gracious, and by God Gabriel had never seen him before - that you sent him To me, he said, while Gabriel remained silent and did not speak until God said: He has spoken the truth, then permission would be given to me in intercession, and I would say: O Lord, your servants, your servants in all parts of the world. Earth, that is the Praiseworthy Place. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” It was sent by Yunus bin Yazid and Mu’mar. Ibn Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, “As for the hadith of Yunus” [p. 615],"
"8702","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yunus told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of a man of knowledge who he did not name, that the earth will expand on the Day of Resurrection. Then he mentioned the hadith similarly, “As for the hadith of Mu’mar.”"
"8703","So Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali ibn Al-Hussein, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The earth will be stretched on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he mentioned something similar, whether\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8701 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8704","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, that Abu Ushanah Al-Maafiri told him that he heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, say: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The sun approaches the earth and people sweat. Among the people are those whose sweat reaches to their ankles, and among them are those whose sweat reaches to the Half of the leg, and some of them reach the knees, and some of them reach the sacrum, and some of them reach the waist, and some It reaches his shoulders, some of them reach his neck, and some of them reach his middle, and he pointed with his hand and he bridled it with his mouth. I saw the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him like this, and among them is someone who is covered by his sweat, and he gestures with his hand and passes his hand over his head without hitting it. “The head was turned with its palm right and left.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8704 - True"
"8705","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abdul Hamid told us Ibn Ja`far, my father told me, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Umair, he said: I sat with Abdullah Ibn Umar and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with them, on the day Friday, and one of them said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Sweat grinds people up,” and one of them said: “Up to the lobes of his ears.” The other said: “He bridles him,” and Ibn Umar said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8705 - True"
"8706","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata informed us, Sa`id reported, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “So that the people of Paradise will be imprisoned on a bridge after they have crossed the path, and some of their injustices that they dealt with in this world will be taken away from each other. Until, when they are cleansed and purified, they will be granted entry into Paradise, for one of them is more knowledgeable about his position in the Hereafter than he is about his position in this world.” He said. Qatada: Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Masoud said: “It is not similar to anything except the people of Jumu’ah who left their Friday prayer.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8706 - True"
"8707","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abdul Rahman told me Bin Maysarah, on the authority of Abu Hani Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited the verse: “On the Day when people will rise up to the Lord of the Worlds” [Al-Muttaffifeen: 6]. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “How? With you, when God gathers you together as arrows are gathered together in a quiver for fifty thousand years, then God does not look at you. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8707 - True"
"8708","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Laythi told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Al-Zubair, may God be pleased with them both, he said: When this verse and this Surah were revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: {Indeed, you will die. And they will die, and then on the Day of Resurrection you will dispute with your Lord.} [Az-Zumar: 31] Al-Zubair said: O Messenger of God, will what was between us be repeated to us? The world with the characteristics of sins? He said: “Yes, that will be repeated to you until each person gets his due.” Al-Zubayr said: “By God, the matter is severe.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8708 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8709","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqqi told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Awf Al-Shaybani said: I heard Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them, saying: We lived for a while and did not see this verse. It was revealed only about us and the People of the Book: {Indeed, you are dead and they are dead. Then on the Day of Resurrection you will dispute before your Lord} [Az-Zumar: 31]. So I said: “We dispute, but we do not worship anyone but God, and as for our religion, it is Islam, and as for our book, it is the Qur’an. We will never change or distort. As for our qiblah, it is the Kaaba, and as for our forbidden or forbidden, it is one, and as for our Prophet, it is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, so how can we dispute until we struggle? “We hit each other’s faces with swords, so I knew that it had been revealed about us.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8709 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8710","Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Hairi told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Shaybani told me, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Quta’i told me, Yahya bin Rashid Al-Mazni, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Nafi’ bin Al-Azraq, on the authority of the Almighty, the Most High, saying: {This is a day when they will not speak} [Al-Mursalat: 35] and {You will not hear except a whispering} {And they turned toward one another. They wonder} [Al-Saffat: 27] and {Go, read his book} So what is this? He said: “Woe to you, have you asked anyone about this before me?” He said: No, he said: “But if you had asked, you would have perished. Did not God, Blessed and Most High, say: ‘And indeed, a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of Do you count} [Al-Hajj: 47]? “He said: Yes, and for every portion of one of these days there is one of these colours.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8710 - Yahya’s weak weakness"
"8711","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, saying: I heard Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah, saying: “ I asked Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi about the reason for the death of Abdullah bin Wahb, and he said: The Book of Horrors was being read to him, so it was read to him. “There was news that he fell unconscious, so we carried him and brought him into the house, and he remained sick until he died, may God be pleased with him.”"
"8712","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, al-Nufaili told us, Musa ibn Ayan told us, on the authority of Laith ibn Abi Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “I will be the master of the people on the day of Resurrection, they will call upon me, my Lord, and I will say: I am Your Lord and Your happiness. Blessed be Your Lord and Your compassion. The Mahdi is the one whom You have guided, and Your servant is in Your hands, there is no refuge. And there is no refuge from you except to you. Blessed are you, the Lord of the House.” He said: “And to slander a fortified property is to destroy the work of a hundred years.” It was included by Muslim. A witness"
"8713","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Abu Muawiyah Muhammad bin Khazim told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, who was young, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, may God be pleased with her, who said: I said to Abu al-Darda’: Don’t you want to entertain your guests? What do men want for their hospitality? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, before you is a difficult obstacle that the burdened will not pass through.” So I would like to lighten it. For that obstacle: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8713 - True"
"8714","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jaafar told me in Baghdad, saying: Abdullah ibn Ahmad told us Ibn Hanbal, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, he said: I heard Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrating that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him, he said: “The record will be presented to the man on the Day of Resurrection, and the injustices of the children of Adam will continue to follow him until it remains a good deed, and more will be added to it. Their bad deeds.” He said: She said to him - or he said: So Asim said to him - On the authority of O Abu Uthman, and he said: On the authority of Salman, Saad, and Ibn Masoud until he enumerated Six or seven of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Shu’bah said: So I asked Asim about this hadith and they told me, on the authority of my father. Othman, on the authority of Salman, and Othman bin Attab told me that he heard Abu Othman narrating this on the authority of Salman and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8714 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8715","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam bin Yahya, Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Wahid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with On their authority, he said: I was informed on the authority of a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hadith about retaliation that I had not heard from him, so I bought a camel and strengthened it. He left, then I walked to him for a month until I came to Egypt - or he said: the Levant - so I came to Abdullah bin Unais and said: A hadith that I heard from you, narrate it. I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I did not hear it in retaliation. I was afraid that I would die before I heard it. Abdullah said: I heard it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “The day the servants - or he said: the people - will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised, with nothing with them. Then He will call them. In a voice that can be heard from far away as well as up close: I am the king, I am the judge, none of the people of Paradise should enter. Paradise, and for anyone of the people of Hell there is injustice upon him until I remove him from it, and it is not appropriate for any of the people of Hell to enter Hell, and for anyone who... “The people of Paradise will be oppressed by him until I repel him from it to the point of a blow.” He said: We said: How? We only come to God Almighty naked and barefoot. He said: “With good deeds and bad deeds.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8715 - True"
"8716","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mughirah Al-Qawwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, said: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, the earth will be stretched out, the earth will be stretched out, and God will gather the creatures together.” Mankind, jinn, animals, and wild beasts. When that day comes, God will make retribution among the animals, until the great sheep are sheared from the horns. By goring her, when God finished retribution among the animals, He said to her: Be dust, and she would be dust, and the unbeliever would see her and say: Oh, I wish I were dust. “Its narrations on the authority of the last of them are trustworthy, except that Abu al-Mughirah is unknown, and the companion’s interpretation is supported.”"
"8717","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Muzaki told me about Marw, Abdullah bin Ruh al-Madaini told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, he told us Sadaqa bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Yazid bin Babunus, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “There are three records: a record of which God does not forgive anything, a record of which God does not care at all, and a record of which God does not leave anything. As for the religion from which God does not forgive anything, it is associating partners with God Almighty. God Almighty said: {Indeed, God does not forgive that anyone should be associated with Him. And He forgives anything other than that to whom He wills.} [An-Nisa: 48] As for the judgment about which God never cares at all, it is the servant’s injustice to himself in what is between himself and others. His Lord, and as for the judgment, of which God does not leave anything, the grievances of His servants will inevitably be redressed among them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8717 - It is a weak charity and Ibn Babanus is foolishness in it"
"8718","Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Sahmi, Abbad bin Shaybah Al-Hubti reported, on the authority of Saeed bin Anas, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: There is a Messenger between us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was sitting when we saw him laughing until his folds became visible. Omar said to him: What made you laugh, O Messenger of God, about my father and my mother? He said: “Two men from my nation knelt down before the Lord of Glory, and one of them said: O Lord, take away from me my injustice from my brother.” Then God, Blessed and Most High, said. To the student: How do you treat your brother when nothing of his good deeds remains? He said: O Lord, let him bear some of my burdens. He said: And the eyes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, filled with tears. He, peace and blessings be upon him, cried, then he said: “Indeed, that day is great. The people will need some of their burdens taken away from them.” Then God Almighty said: To the student: “Raise your gaze and look into Paradise.” He raised his head and said: O Lord, I see cities of gold and palaces of gold crowned. With pearls: What prophet is this, or what truth is this, or what martyr is this? He said: This is for the one who paid the price. He said: O Lord, who owns that? He said: You own it. He said: With what? He said: By your pardoning of your brother. He said: O Lord, I have pardoned him. God Almighty said: So take your brother by the hand and admit him to Paradise. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at that time: “Fear God and reconcile matters between you, for God Almighty reconciles between Muslims.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"8719","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dubari told us, Abd informed us Al-Razzaq, Abdullah bin Buhair reported on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever is pleased to look at the Day of Resurrection as if it were an eye’s view, let him recite: When the sun is rounded and when the sky is It split open, and behold, the sky split open. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8719 - True"
"8720","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl narrated to us, Yahya bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata narrated to us, Al-Fadl bin Issa narrated to us. Al-Raqashi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The disgrace On the Day of Resurrection, a person will be so stubborn that he will say: O Lord, for sending me to Hell is easier for me than what I threw, and he will know the severity of it. Torment: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8720 - Al-Fadl is wah"
"8721","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Al-Alaa bin Ziyad, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: We spoke with the Messenger of God One night, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, we talked a lot. He said: Then we went back to our homes, and when the morning came, we went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The prophets were presented to me tonight with followers from her nation, so the Prophet began to come with him.” The three of his people, the Prophet and a group of people with him, the Prophet and a group of people with him, and the Prophet and none of his people with him, until Musa bin Imran was among the people of Israel, and when I saw them, I admired them, so I said: My Lord, who are these? He said: This is your brother Musa bin Imran and those of the Children of Israel who followed him. He said: I said: Lord, where is my nation? Then it was said to me: Look to your right, and behold, the lions of Mecca have blackened the faces of the men. So I said: My Lord, who are these? He said: Your nation. He said: Then it was said to me: Are you satisfied? So I said: Lord, I am satisfied.He said: Then it was said to me: “Indeed, with these seventy thousand will enter Paradise, and there will be no reckoning against them.” He said: So Okasha bin Muhsin, brother of Bani Asad bin Khuzaymah, and he said: O Prophet of God, pray to your Lord to make me one of them. He said: “O God, make him one of them.” Then another man appeared, He said: O Prophet of God, pray to your Lord to make me one of them. He said: Then he said: Okasha preceded you with it. He said: Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. If you are able to be among the seventy, then be among the seventy. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the oppressed. If you are unable And you fell short, so be among the people of the horizon, for I then saw people shaking a lot.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I hope That whoever follows me from my nation will be a quarter of the people of Paradise.” He said: So we said “Allahu Akbar.” Then he said: “I hope that you will be a third.” So we said “Allahu Akbar.” Then we said: “I hope that you will be a third.” So we said “Allahu Akbar.” He said: “I hope that you will be the half.” So we said the takbeer. He said: Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited “A group of the first and a group of the last.” [Al-Waqi’ah: 40] He said: Then the Muslims looked at these seventy and said: We see them as people who were born into Islam and then they continued to practice it until they died. Accordingly, their hadith was transmitted to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,He said: “It is not so, but they are the ones who do not seek enslavement, nor conceal themselves, nor do they seek refuge, but they put their trust in their Lord.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not expel him in this manner.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8721 - True"
"8722","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli told us, Musaddad told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, On the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I mentioned the Fire and cried, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What’s wrong with you, Aisha?” She said: I mentioned the Fire and cried. Will you remember your families on the Day of Resurrection? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for three situations, no one mentions anyone until he knows whether his scale is light or heavy, and when... Books until it is said: {Come, read his two books} until he knows where his book lies - in his right, in his left, or behind his back, and at the Sirat. When He places between the two backs of Hell its edges will be many turrets and many thistles, with which God will imprison whomever He wishes of His creation until it is known whether they will be saved or not. “This is an authentic hadith whose chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two sheikhs, had it not been for the transmission of it between Al-Hasan and Aisha, although the narrations are authentic that Al-Hasan was As a boy, he entered the house of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and Umm Salamah.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8722 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, had it not been for the transmission of it between Al-Hasan and Aisha"
"8723","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Qaisan told us, Amr bin Ali told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Othman bin Al-Aswad told us, Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, he said: We sat with Abdullah bin Amr in Al-Hijr, and he said: “Cry, and if you do not If you knew the knowledge, one of you would have prayed until his back broke and cried until his voice had stopped.” This is a chain of narration. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8723 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8724","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabab, he said: I heard a mujahid speaking, On the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: “If you knew what I know, you would have laughed little and cried much, and you would not have enjoyed food or drink, and when You slept on mattresses, and you abandoned the women, and you went out into the high places, bellowing and crying, and I wished that God had created me as a tree to support.” This is a chain of narration. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8724 - Interrupted"
"8725","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Khaled bin Abdullah Al-Zayadi, narrated it, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Asbahi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “If you knew what I know, you would cry a lot and laugh a little. Hypocrisy will appear, trustworthiness will be removed, mercy will be withheld, and people will be accused.” The trustworthy, and the untrustworthy is entrusted. He has exposed you to excess and cowardice. They said: What are extravagance and cowardice, O Messenger of God? He said: “Trials are like the likes of a dark night.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8725 - True"
"8726","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muwarriq, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I see what You do not see, and I hear what you do not hear. The sky has expanded and has the right to be lowered. There is not in it the space of four fingers unless there is an angel with his forehead prostrating to God, and by God, if you knew what I know, you would have laughed little and cried much, and you would not have enjoyed enjoying women on beds, and you would have gone out to On the ascending hills you resort to God, and I wish that I were a tree to be supported. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8726 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8727","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari told us, Ya`la ibn Ubaid told us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Hamza, on the authority of Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, give me an easy reckoning.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, what is an easy reckoning? He said: “That he should look at his misdeeds and overlook them. Indeed, whoever is destined for judgment on that Day will perish, and whenever a believer befalls him, he will expiate.” May God protect him from his bad deeds, even the thorn that pricked him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. He did not narrate it in this context, and he witnessed it on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8727 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8728","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Musa ibn Harun told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Omar al-Qawariri told us, Harami ibn Amara told us, Al-Harish bin Al-Kharit, Ibn Abi Mulaika narrated to us, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by me while I was I raised my hands and said: O God, give me a simple reckoning. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you know what that reckoning is?” So I said: God Almighty mentioned in His Book {So He will be given an easy account} [Al-Inshiqaq: 8] and He said to me: “O Aisha, indeed, he who is judged will be judged for that.” The passage is between the hands of God Almighty.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8728 - Al-Harish Al-Bukhari said in his hadith, “Nazr.”"
"8729","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The people of Hell who will be least tormented on the Day of On the Day of Resurrection, there will be a man who will be wearing sandals of fire, from which his brain will boil on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. It has evidence on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the words Different: “As for the hadith of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8729 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8730","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told him, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Khattami and Ismail bin Qutaybah Al-Sulami informed us, they said: Thana Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The least tormented by the people of Hell is he who has two sandals and two tents of fire from which his brains boil as The cauldron boils, and he does not see that there is a more severe torment in the Fire than in it, and that it is the lightest of them in torment.”"
"8731","And Sheikh Abu Bakr told us, Musa bin Ishaq and Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, they said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, told us Abu Usama, on the authority of Al-A’mash, said: I heard Khaythamah. This hadith is also mentioned on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8730 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8732","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Muhammad told me, he said: Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq saying: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, giving a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “The least tormented by the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who will have coals placed on the soles of his feet from which his brain will boil.” Authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8732 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8733","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told me, Saeed bin Masoud told me, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, the people of Hell who will be least tormented on the Day of “The Resurrection will be a man with two coals on the soles of his feet, from which his brain will boil just as a kettle and a bottle boil.” As for the hadith of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri:"
"8734","So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The most despicable of the people of Hell are A man will be tormented on the Day of Resurrection wearing sandals made of fire from which his brain will boil, and among them will be in the fire up to his knees with parts of The torment, and among them is he who is on his garments with the parts of the torment, and among them is he who is up to his collarbones with the parts of the torment, and among them “Whoever has been immersed” in it, this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not take it out. As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas,\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8734 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8735","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz in Hamadan told us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn ibn Dizil told us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas told us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas told us. Hammad, Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The person who is least to be punished is Abu Talib, and on his feet are sandals of fire from which his brain boils.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not \"He takes him out\"\nThey only agreed on the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of al-Abbas, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger By God, Abu Talib used to surround you, prevent you, and get angry with you. Did you help him? He said: “I found him in a cloud of fire, so I brought him out into a clearing.”\nAnd the hadith of Yazid bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubab, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioning his uncle to him. Abu Talib said: “Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will be placed in a pool of fire that will reach his ankles, from which his brain will boil.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8735 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8736","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz and Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us: They said: Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Abdi, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Hisham bin Saad told us, Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: I said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: “Do you have any trouble seeing the sun at noon when it is clear and there are no clouds?” So we said: No, O Messenger of God. He said: “Do you have any trouble seeing the full moon when it is clear and there are no clouds over it?” They said: No. He said: “You will not be harmed in seeing him on the Day of Resurrection except as you would be harmed in seeing one of them, when on the Day of Resurrection he calls Calling: “Let every nation catch up with what it used to worship,” so that no one who worshiped an idol, an idol, or an image will remain except that they will go away until they fall into the Fire. And whoever used to worship God alone will remain, whether righteous or immoral, and the dusty people of the People of the Book. Then Hell will appear as if it were a mirage, destroying each other. Some, then the Jews will be called and he will say: What were you worshiping? They will say: Uzair is the son of God. He will say: You have denied that God has taken a companion as a companion. And there is no child, so what do you want? They say: Yes, our Lord, give us drink. He says: Why do you not want? So they go until they fall into the Fire.Then the Christians will be called and He will say: What were you worshiping? They will say: The Messiah, the Son of God. He will say: You have lied. God has not taken a companion or A son, what do you want? So they say: Yes, our Lord, give us drink. So He says: Will you not? So they go until they fall into the Fire, leaving only those who worshiped God alone. From the righteous and the immoral. Then God appears to us in an image other than the image in which we saw him the first time, and He says: O people, every nation has caught up with what She used to worship and you remained, and no one will speak to him on that day except the prophets, and they will say: We separated from the people in this world while we were in their company in it. In need, every nation has caught up with what it used to worship, and we are waiting for our Lord whom we used to worship. He will say: I am your Lord. So they will say: We seek refuge in God. From you, and He says: Is there between you and God any sign that you know? So they say: What a good leg. Then a leg is revealed and everyone falls down in prostration, and no one remains who had prostrated in this world out of reputation, hypocrisy, or hypocrisy except for the sake of His back was one layer. Whenever he wanted to prostrate, he fell on his back. He said: Then our righteous and our wrongdoer will be taken away, and he has returned to us in his form that we saw. The first time, he will say: I am your Lord, and they will say: Yes, you are our Lord three times, then the bridge over Hell will be struck.We said: What is the connection, O Messenger of God, with our father and our mother? He said: A slippery slope that has hooks, hooks, and thistles with an onyx rock, and it is called Al-Sa’dan. The believer passes by like a flash of lightning, and like a thorn. And like the wind, and like birds, and like the backs of horses and chariots, a broken and scratched cup is sent and piled up in the fire of hell, and by the One in whose hand is my soul. Is there one of you who is more severe than us in fulfilling the truth that the believers see in their brothers? When they see them saved from the Fire, they say: That is, our Lord. Our brothers were praying with us, fasting with us, performing Hajj with us, and fighting with us. The fire took them, and God, Blessed, says And God Almighty: Go, and bring out whoever’s appearance you know, and their images will be burnt over the fire, and the man will be found. The fire has taken him to his feet, and to the He cut his legs, and his knees, and his loins, and they came out of them as human beings. Then they spoke again, and he continued to say to them until... He says: Go and bring out whoever in whose heart you find an atom’s weight of goodness, take him out. So, when Abu Sa’id narrated this, The hadith says: If you do not believe it, then read {Indeed, God does not do wrong even the weight of an atom, and if it is a good deed, He will multiply it and give from Himself a great reward} [An-Nisa: 40] Then they say: “Our Lord, we have not left in it any good.He says: Is there anyone left except the Most Merciful of the merciful? The angels have interceded and the prophets have interceded. Is there anything left but the Most Merciful of the merciful? He said: Then he takes a handful of the fire and brings out a people who have returned to being a group of people who have never done any good work for him, and they are thrown into a river called Nahr. Life, so they grow therein, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, just as a seed grows in the depths of a torrent. Have you not seen it and the yellow shadow that follows it and what follows it? Is it greener than the sun? He said: We said: O Messenger of God, it is as if you were among the livestock. He said: They will sprout in this manner and come out like pearls placed around their necks. Then they will be sent into Paradise, and the people of Paradise will say: These are the infernal ones whom He brought out of Hell without any work. They did it, but there was no good they offered. God Almighty says: Take, and you will have what you have taken. So they take until they stop, then they say: God Almighty will not give us. And whenever We take, God, Blessed and Most High, says: Indeed, I have given you better than what you have taken, and they say: Our Lord, and what is better than that? And from what did we take? Ridwani said without anger, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.” Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Al-Musayyab, and Ata’ Ibn Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah briefly,Muslim alone narrated the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, with less than Half of this is driving"
"8737","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Othman bin Ghayath al-Rasibi reported that Abu Nadhrah told them, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The people will be gathered at the bridge of Hell with thorns and hooks on it, and the people will pass by, and some of them will pass by like lightning, and some of them will pass like lightning. The galloping horse, some of them running, some of them walking, some of them crawling, and the angels at his sides say: O God, grant us peace. And the dogs snatch them up. He said: As for its people, who are its people, they neither die nor live, but as for people who are captured for sins. And their sins will be burned up and become charcoal, then they will be captured in a scattering of dust and thrown onto a river from Paradise, and they will sprout as it sprouts. “The grain in the flow of the torrent.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have you seen the dye? Then after that permission will be given to them and they will enter Paradise.” Abu Sa’id said: Then one of them will be given something like this world. He said: “And on the path there are three Trees, and the last person to emerge from the fire will be on their edge and say: O Lord, bring me to this tree, so that I may be in its shade and eat of its fruit. He said: So he says: Your covenant and my covenant, do not ask me for anything else. So he says: My covenant and my covenant, I do not ask anything else. Then he changes it to it and sees another, better one. And he says: O Lord, I will eat of its fruit and be in its shade. Then he will change to it, then he will see another that is better than it, and he will say: O Lord. I will eat of its fruit and be in its shade, and he will be turned to it. He said: Then he will hear the voices of the people and see their crowds, and he will say: O Lord, let me in. “Paradise.” Abu Sa’id said: Then he mentioned the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned it, and one of them said: “He will be given something like the world.” And the like of it with it.” Another said: “The like of this world and ten times like it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8737 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8738","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, Abdullah bin Al-Mughirah bin Muaqib narrated to me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr Al-Awari, Laith narrated to me, and he was in my father’s lap. Saeed, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The path will be placed between the two backs of Hell.” He will have a thorn like the thorn of a monkey. Then the people will seek protection from a safe and wounded animal with which it is kept, and it will be contained in an inverted climate. Then, when God Almighty has finished with Issues between the servants, and the believers visited men who in this world were praying their prayers, paying their zakat, and observing their fasts. And they perform their Hajj, and they perform their own battle, and they say: Oh, our Lord, are servants of Your servants who were in this world with us, praying with our prayers, and purifying themselves. Our zakat, and they fast our fast, and they perform our Hajj, and they fight our battle, but we do not see them. He said: He says: Go to Hell, for whoever you find in it. So they took him out. He said: They will find them and the fire has taken them according to their deeds. Some of them took him to his feet, and some of them took him to his feet. She took it to his knees, and some of them to his lower garment, and some of them she took to his breasts, and some of them she took to his neck, and she did not The faces will be obscured. He said: Then they will bring them out and throw them into the water of life. It was said: O Prophet of God, what is the water of life? He said: “The people of Paradise will be washed and they will sprout therein just as a plant sprouts in the scum of a torrent. Then the prophets will intercede for everyone who testified that There is no god but God, sincere, so they will extract them from it, then God will be compassionate with His mercy on those who are in it, so He will not leave anyone in his heart therein. “An atom’s weight of faith except that He took it out of it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, but He did not take it out of it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8738 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8739","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair told us, Hadba bin Khalid told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The scale will be placed on the Day of Resurrection, and if the heavens and the earth were weighed, it would expand. Then the angels say: O Lord, to whom is this weighed? Then God Almighty says: To whomsoever I will of My creation. Then the angels say: Glory be to You. We have not worshiped You with the right to worship You. And the path will be laid out like the edge of a razor. Then the angels say: Who do you allow for this? He says: Whoever you wish from among My creation, and He says: Glory be to You, we have not worshiped You with the right to worship You. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8739 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8740","Muhammad bin Tahir bin Yahya told me, my father told me, Ahmad bin Hafs told me, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Bahili, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Indeed, among the people of Hell are those whom the Fire will take to his ankles, and among them are those whom it will take to his knees, and among them are those “You take him to the hold, and some of them take him to the collarbone.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8740 - True"
"8741","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, He said: I once asked about the Almighty’s saying: {And there is not among you except the one who will go to it} [Maryam: 71], so he told me that Abdullah bin Masoud told them that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People fight the Fire and then escape from it by their deeds. At first they are like a flash of lightning, then like the wind, then Like the mount of a horse, then like a rider on his mount, then the pull of a man, then like his walking.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. Narrated by Shu`bah, on the authority of Ismail al-Suddi.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8741 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8742","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Awwam told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, On the authority of Abdullah: {And there is not among you but he who will enter it} [Maryam: 71]. He said: “They return it, then they turn away from it with their deeds.”"
"8743","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Nasa’i told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah: {And there is not one of you except Mary who will go to her} [Maryam: 71] He said: “They return it, then they turn away from it with their own deeds.” He said Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: So Shu`bah narrated, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, with a chain of transmission traceable to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, but I deliberately left him alone"
"8744","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, and Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, they said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, Abu Salih Ghalib bin Sulaiman bin Harb told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Ziyad Abi Sahl, on the authority of Minyat al-Azdiya, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shaybah, he said: We disagreed here about the flowers, and some people said: No believer will enter them, and others said: They will all enter them, then God will save those who Beware of fear, so I said to him: We disagreed over it in Basra, and some people said: No believer will enter it, and others said: They will enter it all, and then God will save. Those who fear God. Then he leaned his two fingers to his ears and said: Be silent if I did not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The Roses.” Entry Neither the righteous nor the immoral will remain except that he enters it, and it will be coolness and peace for the believer just as it was for Abraham, to the point of Hell - or he said: Hell - “Noisy from her bleeding.” Then he said: “Then Allah will save those who feared Him and leave the wrongdoers therein crouching.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8744 - True"
"8745","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Jarrah Al-Adl told us about Marwa, Yahya bin Sasawayh told us, Ali bin Hajr told us, Dawud told us Ibn Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Ismail Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, that Ibn Masoud was asked about the saying of God Almighty: {And there is not among you except those who enter it.} [Maryam: 71] He said: “And there is not among you except those who enter it. It is a definite decree from your Lord; then God will save those who feared. “And He will leave the wrongdoers therein crouching.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8745 - Dawud bin Al-Zubur was left by Abu Dawud"
"8746","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari and Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us Al-Abdi, Ubaid bin Ubaidah Al-Qurashi narrated to us, Al-Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father, saying: Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abd. Al-Ghafir, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let a man take his father’s hand on the Day of On the Day of Resurrection, Hell will engulf him. He wants to admit him to Paradise. He said: Then he will be called: Indeed, no polytheist will enter Paradise. Indeed, God has forbidden Paradise to Every polytheist, he said: Then he says: Oh, my Lord, my father. Then he is transformed into an ugly form and a foul odor and leaves him. “He said: So the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him: “They see that it is Abraham, peace be upon him, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not add anything to them on that.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not take it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8746 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8747","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Sa’id bin Muhammad Al-Hajwani told us, in Kufa, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, Ismail bin Abi told us Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: “Abdullah bin Rawahah cried and his wife cried, so he said: What makes you cry? She said: I saw you crying.” So I cried. He said: I was told that I would bring it, but I was not told that I would take it. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8748","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul-Hamid Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, Abd al-Razzaq reported, Ibn Uyaynah reported, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais ibn Abi Hazim, who said: “Abdullah ibn Rawaha put his head on his wife’s lap and wept, and his wife wept, so he said: What makes you cry? She said: I saw you crying, so I cried. He said: I remembered the words of God Almighty: {And there is not one of you except one who will go to it} [Maryam: 71], so I do not know whether I will be saved. Whether or not it is “this hadith is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8748 - There is a transmission"
"8749","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abu Malik told us Saad bin Tariq Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rab’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, and Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: “God will gather the people, and the believers will rise up when Paradise approaches. They will go to Adam, peace and blessings be upon him, and say: O our father, open For us is Paradise. He says: Did anything take you out of Paradise except the sin of your father Adam? I am not the owner of that. Baptize Abraham, the friend of God. So they came to Abraham, and Abraham said: I am not that man's friend, but I was a friend from back to back. Baptize the Prophet Moses, to whom God spoke. Speaking, they came to Moses, and he said: I am not that companion. Go to the word of God and His Spirit, Jesus, and Jesus said: I am not that companion. Then they will come to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he will stand up and permission will be given to him, and trust and mercy will be sent with him, and they will stand on the path, right and left, and he will pass. The first of you are like the lightning flashing.” I said: May my mother and father be sacrificed for anything that the lightning flashed. He said: “Have you not seen how the lightning passes and then comes back in the blink of an eye, then it flashes The wind, the bitterness of the birds, and the strength of the mounts, their deeds will be carried out by them, and your Prophet is standing on the path, my Lord, peace and peace. He said: Until the deeds of the people become impossible until He comes. The man cannot pass except by crawling. He said: And at both edges of the path there are hooks hanging, commanded to take whomever they command, and he is scratched and saved. And he will be buried in Hell. “By the One in whose Hand is Abu Hurairah’s soul, the bottom of Hell is for seventy autumns.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8749 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8750","Abu Al-Qasim Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He will meet A man will see his father on the Day of Resurrection, and he will say to him: O father, what kind of son have I been to you? He says: The best son. Then he says: Are you obedient to me today? So he says: Yes, then he says: Take my overalls, and he takes his own overalls, then goes off until God, Blessed and Most High, comes and presents creation. He says: O my servant, enter through any gate of Paradise you wish. He says: Yes, my Lord, and my father is with me, for you promised me that you would not disgrace me. He said: Then God will transform his father into a hyena, and he will turn away from him and fall into the Fire, and will be caught by the nose. Then God, Blessed and Most High, will say: O my servant, your father. Him? So he says: No, by Your glory, “this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8750 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8751","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani told me about Kufa from the origin of his book. Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza al-Ghifari told us, Malik bin Ismail Al-Nahdi told us, Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, Yazid bin Abdul Rahman Abu Khalid Al-Dalani told us, Al-Minhal bin told us Amr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and a herald will call: O people, are you not satisfied with your Lord who created you, fashioned you, and provided for you to be loyal to every person? A person who was not worshiped in this world and turned away. Isn’t that justice from your Lord? They said: Yes. He said: Then each one of you will go to what he used to follow in this world and represent to them what they used to worship in this world. And he said: He will represent. To those who worshiped Jesus, the devil of Jesus appeared, and to those who worshiped Uzair, the devil of Uzair appeared to them, until the tree, the stick, and the stone appeared to them, and the people of Islam crouched down and said to them: Why do you not set out as the people did? And they say: Indeed, we have a Lord whom we have not yet seen. He said: Then He says: How will you know your Lord if you see Him? They said: There is a sign between us and him. If we see him, we recognize him. He said: What is it? They said: the leg.Then a leg will be uncovered. He said: Then everyone who has their backs will bow down and prostrate, while some people will remain with their backs like cows hunting down. They want to prostrate, but they do not They are able. He said: Then they are commanded to raise their heads and are given their light in proportion to their deeds. Among them are those whose light is given like a mountain. between His hands, and among them is he who is given his light other than that, and among them is he who is given his light like a palm tree in his right hand, and among them is he who is given even less than that. At the end of that, his light will be given on his big toe. It will shine sometimes and go out sometimes. When it shines, he steps forward, and when it goes out, he stands. They will pass by. The path, and the path is like the edge of a sword, rebutting a slip. He said: Then it will be said, “Save according to the measure of your light.” And among them are those who pass by like the passing of a star, and among them are those. It passes like a wind, and some of them passes like the wind, and some of them passes like a saddlebag and covers sand, so they pass according to their deeds, until He whose light passes. On the thumb of his foot, he drags a hand and hangs a hand, and drags a foot and hangs a foot, and fire hits his sides. He said: Then they will be saved. And when they are saved, They said: Praise be to God who saved us from you after we saw you. God has given us what He has not given anyone else. So they go to Dahdah at the door of Paradise, and he is facing a dwelling in the nearest part of Paradise, and they say: Our Lord, give us that dwelling.He said: Then he will say to them: You ask me for Paradise while he is standing still, and I have saved you from Hell. They will not hear the sound of this gate. So he will say to them: Perhaps, if you give it to him, you will ask Me for something else. He said: And he says: No, by Your glory, we do not ask You for anything else. And what abode is better than it? He said: So they will give it to him, and in front of that another station will be raised for them, as if what they were given before that had a dream with those who saw it. He said: Then he says: To them: Perhaps, if you were given it, you would ask Me for something else. They would say: No, by Your glory, we do not ask You for anything else. And what abode is better than it? They will be given it and then remain silent. He said: Then it will be said to them: Why do you not ask me? They say: Our Lord, we have asked until we became ashamed. He said: Then He says to them: Would you not be satisfied if I gave you something like the world from the day I created it? Until the day it is consumed and ten times it.” He said: Masruq said: Abdullah did not reach this place in the conversation except he laughed, he said: So he said He has a man: O Abu Abdul Rahman, I have been told this hadith many times, and I have never reached this place in this hadith without laughing.He said: Then Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrating this hadith repeatedly, but this hadith has not reached this place. Except that he laughed until his mouth became apparent and the last of his molars appeared, as the human being said: “Are you mocking me when you are the king?” He said: “Then the Lord, Blessed and Most High, will say, ‘No, but I am able to do that, so ask me.’ He said: ‘And they will say: Our Lord, join us with the people.’ So He will say to them: ‘Follow With the people, he said: Then they go off and spend their time in Paradise until a man among them appears to be a palace made of a hollow pearl. He said: Then he falls down, prostrating. He said: Then it is said to him: Raise your head, and he raises his head, and it is said: This is only one of your dwellings. He said: So he goes off and a man meets him and says: Are you a king? It will be said: “That is only a Kahraman from your Qahārīmah, a slave from your servants.” He said: Then he will come to him and say: I am only a Qāhramān from your Qāḥarīmah over This palace is under the hands of a thousand rulers, all of them as I am. He said: Then he will proceed with it until the palace is opened while it is a jewel. Its roofs, doors, locks, and keys are hollow, so the palace opens for him and he is greeted by a green jewel lined with It is seventy cubits long and has sixty gates, each gate leading to a single jewel of a different color than its owner.In every jewel there are secrets, pairs, and descriptions - or he said: and descriptions - he said: Then he enters, and behold, he is in Hawraa, a spring covered with seventy robes. He can see The marrow of her leg, behind her robe, her liver is his mirror, and his liver is her mirror. If he turned away from her, it would increase in his eyes seventy-fold. than what happened before that. He says: You have increased in my eyes seventy-fold. And you say to him like that. He said: Then he looks over his kingdom. A journey of one hundred years.” He said: Then Omar said at that: O Ka’b, do you not listen to what Ibn Umm Abd tells us about the lowest wealth among the people of Paradise? So what about the highest ones? He said: “O Commander of the Faithful, no eye has seen, no ear has heard. Indeed, God was above the throne and the water, and He created for Himself an abode with His own hand and beautified it.” whatever He wished, and He placed in it fruits and drinks, then He closed it, and none of His creation has seen it since the day He created it, neither Gabriel nor anyone else. the angels, then Ka’b recited, so no soul knows what has been hidden from them of the comfort of eyes. And apart from that He created two gardens and decorated them with whatever He wished and made In them is what was mentioned of silk, silk, and brocade, and He showed them to whomsoever He willed of His creation from among the angels. So whoever’s book was in the two highest places will be seen in that house,So, if a man from the people of Aliyin rides in his kingdom, he will not stay in one of the tents of Paradise without entering it by the light of his face. They inhale its scent and say: What a pleasant scent, and they say: Today a man from the people of Illiyan supervised us. Omar said: Woe to you, O Ka’b! Indeed, these hearts have become lest, so seize them. So Ka’b said: “O Commander of the Faithful, indeed Hell has a pit. There is no angel close to it, nor A prophet does not prostrate himself on his knees until Abraham, the friend of God, says: Lord of my soul, my soul, and even if you have the work of seventy prophets, I will continue your work. You would have thought that you would not be saved from it.” The narrators of this hadith from the last of them are trustworthy, except that they did not narrate Abu Khaled al-Dalani in the two Sahihs because He was mentioned regarding his deviation from the Sunnah in mentioning the Companions. As for the previous imams, they all testified to Abu Khaled’s truthfulness and perfection. The hadith is authentic, and it was not narrated by Abu Khaled al-Dalani, who is one of those whose hadith is collected among the imams of the people of Kufa.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8751 - What he denied recently based on the quality of its chain of transmission"
"8752","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abd al-A’la bin Abd told us The highest, Dawud bin Abi Hind narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais, who said: I was submitting the judge to Abu Burdah, so I was with him and he entered upon him. Al-Harith bin Qais was with him and he was with him, so he narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There are not two Muslims who die except four. May God admit them to Paradise by the grace of His mercy to them. We said: O Messenger of God, and three? He said: “And three.” We said: O Messenger of God, and two. He said: “And two.” Then he said: “Indeed, among my nation is one who is placed in the Fire until he is one of its corners. “And indeed, among my nation, there will be more than one who will enter Paradise through his intercession.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8752 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8753","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Mandah Al-Asbahani told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Hussein bin Farqad told us, Al-Hasan told us, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “This fire of yours is one part out of seventy parts of fire.” Hell, and had it not been dipped in water twice, you would not have enjoyed it. “She seeks God’s protection - that he will never put her back in the Fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it in this context.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8753 - Hassan Wah"
"8754","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj Abi Al-Samh, that he heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Juz’ Al-Zubaidi, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, in the Fire are serpents like the necks of a camel. One of them will bite with the sting and will find its fire for forty autumns.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it is not \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8754 - True"
"8755","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu Qalaba told us, Bishr bin Amr Al-Zahrani told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, On the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, in the words of God Almighty: {We have increased for them a punishment beyond the punishment} [An-Nahl: 88] He said: “The scorpions with their tusks are like tall palm trees.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8755 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8756","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdullah bin Abbas told me, he told me Abdullah bin Suleiman, on the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Issa bin Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, between the two lands, between every earth is a journey of five hundred years, and the highest of them is on the back of A whale whose two sides met in the sky, and the whale was on its back on a rock, and the rock was in the hand of an angel, and the second was harnessing the wind, so when God wanted to He commanded the treasurer of the wind to send upon them a wind that would destroy the enemy. He said: O Lord, send upon them a wind equal to the size of an ox’s nostril. Then the mighty man said to him. Blessed and Most High: Then the earth and those upon it are sufficient, but send upon them as much as a seal, and it is what God Almighty said in His Mighty Book: {She does not leave out of anything upon which she has come but that she has made it like rubble.} [Al-Dhariyat: 42], and the third in it are the stones of Hell, and the fourth in it is the sulfur of Hell.” They said: O Messenger of God, does fire contain brimstone? He said: “Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, therein are valleys of sulphur. If one were to send into them firm mountains, they would sparkle, and the fifth therein are snakes.” Hell, its mouths are like valleys that sting the disbeliever with stinging, so that no flesh remains of him on bone. And the sixth place therein is the scorpions of Hell. The slightest scorpion of it is like trussed mules, striking the infidel with a blow that makes him forget its blow, the heat of Hell, and the seventh is sunk, and in it is Satan. Shackled with iron, one hand in front of him and one hand behind him, so if God wanted to release him to whomever He wished of His servants, He would release him.” This is a hadith that was unique to him. Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Issa bin Hilal, and I mentioned his justice in the text of Imam Yahya bin Ma’in, may God be pleased with him, and the hadith is authentic. And they did not take him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8756 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"8757","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Yahya al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir informed us, Ya`la ibn Ubaid informed us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abbad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him On her authority, she said: “When this verse was revealed in Al-Muzzammil: {And leave me and the deniers who are the recipients of blessing, and give them respite a little. Indeed, with Us is a punishment. And Hell.} [Al-Muzzammil: 12] It was only a short time until the battle of Badr occurred. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n Shibl, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And juicy food} [Al-Muzzammil: 13], he said: “The tree of Zaqqum.” Authentic.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8757 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8758","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told us, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told us, Amr ibn Hafs ibn Ghayath told us, Ubayy told us, Al-Alaa ibn Khalid told us. Al-Kahili, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Hell will be brought on that day and it will “Seventy thousand reins, with each reins seventy thousand angels pulling them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8758 - But Al-Ala was denied by Abu Maslamah Al-Tabudhaki."
"8759","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The molar of an infidel On the Day of Resurrection, he will be like Uhud, and the width of his skin will be seventy cubits, and his upper arm will be like white paper, and his thigh will be like a leaf, and his seat in the Fire will be as long as “Between me and Al-Rabdha” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, they agreed to mention the molar of the infidel only.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8759 - True"
"8760","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shayban told us, about Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The skin of an infidel is as thick as two And forty cubits are equal to the cubits of the mighty, and his tooth is like Uhud.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “Sheikh Abu said Bakr, may God be pleased with him: The meaning of his saying “with the arm of the mighty”: “that is, a mighty of the mighty of human beings who existed in the first centuries, who was greater.” He has the longest limbs and cubits of human beings.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8760 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8761","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of my father Hilal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: “The molar tooth of the infidel on the Day of Resurrection Like Uhud, his head is like white, his thigh is like two leaves, and his skin is seventy cubits thick, and his seat in Hell is as Medina and Al-Rabdha.” Abu Hurairah said: “And it was said, ‘His belly is like the belly of Idham.’ This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He takes it out to confiscate it to Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8761 - Suspended"
"8762","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah told us, Safwan bin Ya’la told me that Ya’la said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sea is hell.” They said to Ali: He said God Almighty said: {A fire whose curtain surrounds them} [Al-Kahf: 29] And He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will never enter it until I meet God, and I will not be afflicted by it from it.” A drop” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and its meaning is that the sea is difficult as if it were hell, and therefore it is a branch of the narration of the hadith of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that under the sea is fire, and under fire is a sea, as for fire, it is under the seventh, and he testified The Companions and those after them upon seeing its smoke.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8762 - True"
"8763","As Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar told us, Abdullah bin Fayrouz Al-Danaj told me, Talq bin Habib told me, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “I saw smoke coming from Al-Darar Mosque when it collapsed.” This is an authentic chain of narration, and a group of our strange friends told me that they knew this. The mosque and they saw this smoke, and I presented the correct narration that Hell is under the seventh earth.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8763 - True"
"8764","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj, On the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Woe to the valley in Hell in which the disbeliever falls.” Forty autumns before it reaches its bottom, and ascending a mountain in the Fire is seventy autumns from which it will fall. This is the case forever.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8764 - True"
"8765","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, dictating from the original of his book, Ibrahim bin Ubayd Allah Al-Saadi told us, Yazid told us Ibn Harun, Azhar Ibn Sinan Al-Qurashi informed us, Muhammad Ibn Wasi’ narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Bilal Ibn Abi Burdah and said to him: O Bilal. Your father told me on the authority of your grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Indeed, in Hell is a valley. In that valley is a well called “Habhab, it is the duty of God Almighty that every mighty man should make it quiet.” So beware of being one of them, O Bilal. “This is a hadith narrated alone by Azhar ibn Sinan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, “Ali did not write it except from this narration.”"
"8766","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Azhar bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj, On the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A monument will be erected for the infidel on the Day of Resurrection.” The amount of fifty thousand years, as he did not do in this world, and he thinks that he will defend him. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8766 - True"
"8767","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Aziz Al-Aili informed me, Salama told them, on the authority of Aqeel, Ibn Shihab told me, that Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, what is between the edge of the Fire and its bottom is like a rock weighing seven With their fat, their flesh, and their children, they will fall between the edge of the Fire and its bottom until it reaches its bottom in seventy autumns.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8767 - True"
"8768","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Aziz Al-Aili informed me, Salamah, he told them, on the authority of Aqeel, Ibn Shihab told me, that Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, said: Abu Huraira: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the distance between the edge of the Fire and its bottom is decreed until it falls.” Its bottom is seventy autumns.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"8769","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Yazid bin Harun told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim informed me Al-Taymi, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A man may speak By a word, one does not think that it will reach what it has reached, and it will be thrown into Hell for seventy years.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8769 - True"
"8770","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed informed us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, in the Almighty’s saying: {And call out, O Master, that your Lord may destroy us} [Al-Zukhruf: 77] He said: “He clears He did not answer them for forty years, then he answered them: {Indeed, you are tarrying} [Al-Zukhruf: 77] and they say: {Our Lord, remove us from it. If we return Indeed, we are wrongdoers.} [Al-Mu’minun: 107] He said: So he will give away from them something like this world. Then He answered them: “Be wrong in it and do not speak.” He said: By God, what The people do not speak after this word, except for exhaling and inhaling. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8770 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8771","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Darraj Abi Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The seat of the infidel is among the The Fire is a distance of three days, and every tooth is like a tooth, and his thigh is like two leaves, and his skin except his flesh and his bones is forty cubits.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8771 - True"
"8772","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Asad bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan bin Saeed, Salamah bin Kuhail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, he said: The Antichrist was mentioned to Abdullah, and he said: “The people will separate into three groups when he emerges: A group will follow him, a group will join its people in the wormwood beds, and a group will take the shore of this Euphrates. He will fight them and they will fight him until they are killed. In the west of the Levant, they would send a vanguard among them a blond - or pale - horse - and they would kill each other, but none of them would return. He said: Abu told me Sadiq, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najid, that it is a blond horse. He said: The People of the Book claim that Christ, peace be upon him, will descend and kill him. And Gog and Magog will come out, and they will slip away from every direction, and God will send against them an animal like a palm tree, and it will sink into their ears and their nostrils. They will die, and the earth will stink because of them, and they will be summoned to God Almighty and He will send water and purify the earth of them, and God will send a wind into it. It is a cold wind, so do not leave a believer on the earth except that that wind suffocates him. Then the Hour will come upon the wickedest of people. Then an angel will arise in the sky. And the earth, and it is blown into it, and there remains nothing of God’s creation in the heavens and the earth except that he dies, except whom your Lord wills.Then between the two blasts there will be as long as God wills, and there is not one of the children of Adam except that there is some of him on earth. Then God will send water from under the Throne like a rainwater. men, and their flesh and their bodies will sprout just as the earth sprouts from the dirt. Then Abdullah recited: {It is God who sends the winds and they stir up the clouds. So We drove him to a dead land} until he reached {Thus is the Resurrection} [Fatir: 9] Then an angel will stand between the heaven and the earth and blow into it and all will go forth. A soul enters its body and enters it, and they rise and come as one man rises for the Lord of the worlds. Then God Almighty will appear to creation. Then he meets the Jews and says: Who do you worship? They say: We worship Uzair. He says: Does water please you? They said: Yes, so he would show them Hell and it was like a mirage. Then Abdullah recited: “And We will display Hell that Day to the disbelievers as a display” [Al-Kahf: 100]. Then he meets the Christians and says: Who do you worship? They say: We worship Christ. He says: Does water please you? They say: Yes, so he shows them Hell, which is like a mirage. Then likewise whoever worships anything besides God,Then Abdullah recited {Stop them, indeed they will be questioned} [Al-Saffat: 24] until the Muslims remained and said: Who do you worship? They say: We worship God and do not associate anything with Him. Then he rebuked them two or three times: Who do you worship? They say: We worship God and do not associate anything with Him. Then He says: Do you know your Lord? They say: When He confesses to us, Glory be to Him, we recognize Him. Then a leg will be revealed, and no believer will remain except that he prostrates himself before God, and he will remain. The hypocrites have one side of their backs as if there were footsteps in it, and they say: Our Lord. He says: You were called to prostrate while you were They are safe. Then God will command the path and it will be set upon Hell, so people will pass by in groups according to their deeds. The first of them are like the flash of lightning, then like the passing of the wind. Then the birds passed, then the animals, until a man passed running, then a man passed walking, until the last of them came, a man rolling on his stomach and saying: Lord, why have you been so slow with me? He said: I did not delay you, but rather your work delayed you. Then God Almighty permits intercession, and the first intercessor will be the Holy Spirit of God. Gabriel, then Abraham, then Moses, then Jesus, then your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, will rise, and no one will intercede for what he intercedes for.It is the Praiseworthy Place that God Almighty mentioned {Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a Praiseworthy Place} [Al-Isra: 79]. There is not a soul that does not wait. To a house in Paradise.” Sufyan said: I think he said: “If you had known the Day when the people of Paradise will see what is in Hell and say: ‘If it had not been from God upon us, then the angels, the prophets, the martyrs, the righteous, and the believers will intercede, and God will intercede for them. Then He will say: I am the Most Merciful of the merciful, and He will come out. From the Fire, more than He brought out all of creation by His mercy, so that no good would be left out of it. Then Abdullah recited {what led you in Saqr} [Al-Muddaththir: 42] And he said: With his hand, he held it. {They said, “We were not of those who prayed, nor did we feed the poor, and we used to quarrel with those who disputed, and we used to deny the Day of Judgment} [Al-Muddaththir: 44] Do you see any good in these people? There is good in whatever is left out of anyone. If God wills not to expel anyone, He changes their faces and colors, then the man comes and intercedes. So he says: Whoever knows someone, let him take him out. Then he comes and does not know anyone, then a man calls him and says: I am so-and-so, and he says: I don’t know you. That is when they said: {Our Lord, remove us from it. But if we return, then we are wrongdoers. He said, “Be humble therein and do not speak to Him.” So when He said that, it applied to them.Not a single one of them came out. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"8773","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If only an iron cone “It was placed in the earth, and the two heavyweights gathered for it what they had taken from the earth.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8773 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8774","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad. He said: It was read to Yahya bin Ja’far bin al-Zabarqan while I was listening. Secondly: Ali bin Asim, Bahz bin Hakim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, I did not come to you Until I left behind more than these, meaning all of my hands, and I will not follow your religion nor will I come to you, and I was a person who did not understand anything except what God taught me. And His Messenger, then I ask you in the face of God: Why has our Lord sent you? He said: “By Islam.” He said: I said: O Prophet of God, what is the sign of Islam? He said: “That you say, ‘I have submitted my face to God,’ and establish prayer, and pay zakat. Every Muslim on behalf of a Muharram Muslim become brothers. God will not accept it.” From a Muslim who commits polytheism after he has converted to Islam until he separates from the polytheists to the Muslims. Why would I take to keep you away from the Fire? Indeed, my Lord is calling me. And He is asking Me: Have you conveyed the message to My servants? And I say: My Lord, I have conveyed to them, so let your witness inform your absent person. Then you will call the front of your mouths with redemption, then the first “One of you shows his thigh and his palm.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, this is our religion, and where do you improve with your palm? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8774 - True"
"8775","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The tent of fire has four walls. “Each wall of it is forty years long.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it."
"8776","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Firas Al-Maliki, the jurist, told us about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded in the Sacred Mosque, Bakr bin Sahl told us. Al-Damiati, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Atiya bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, the muezzin of Jerusalem, He said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, saying: “Indeed, the wall that God Almighty mentioned in the Qur’an {so he put up among them a wall of His own.” A gate whose inside is mercy, and on its outside is punishment.} [Al-Hadid: 13] It is the eastern wall, the inside of which is the mosque and what is next to it, and its outside is a valley. Hell “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8776 - True"
"8777","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Darraj Abi Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a suppressed person hits... “The iron of Hell, the mountain, was crumbled to pieces as the people of Hell are struck by it, and it became ashes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8777 - True"
"8778","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani, may God have mercy on him, told us in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Anbas told us, Ali bin told us Coming, Sharik told us, on the authority of Ubaid Al-Muttab, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, laughed One day he greeted or smiled, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Won’t you ask me about what I laughed about?” He said: “I am amazed at the servant’s argument with his Lord on the Day of Resurrection. He will say: O Lord, did you not promise me that you would not wrong me? He said: Yes, he said: I do not accept the testimony of any witness except from myself. Then he says: Or is not me a sufficient witness and the honorable angels? The writers? He said: Then he repeats these words several times, then he concludes his statement, and its pillars speak of what he used to do, and he says: Far from you and damned, I was away from you. I argue: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8778 - According to the condition and Muslim"
"8779","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a bucket of dusk were spilled “In this world, you are the people of the world.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8779 - True"
"8780","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Amrawayh Al-Saffar told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Mutaraf, speaking that he had two wives, so he came to one of them, and he said: She started to remove His turban and said: Did you come from your wife? He said: I came from Imran bin Husayn, and he narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “The fewest inhabitants of Paradise are women.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8780 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8781","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Jafar Al-Khattimi, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, said: We were with Amr bin Al-Aas on Hajj or Umrah, and when we were passing by Dhahran, We saw a woman in her howdah, with her hand on her howdah, in which were rings. And when the people came down, behold, we saw many crows in her. A red crow with a red beak and feet. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No woman like this will enter Paradise.” “The crow in these crows” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8781 - According to the condition and Muslim"
"8782","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hassan bin Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Asadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Adam bin Ubayy told us Iyas, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Ja’far Al-Khutmi told us, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, he said: We were with Amr bin Al-Aas on Hajj. Or Umrah, then suddenly there was a woman with her rings in her hand and she had placed her hand on her howdah. Then Amr ibn al-Aas entered a group, then he said: We were with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among this people, and behold, there were many crows, and behold, a single, black crow with a red beak and feet. Then the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “No woman will enter Paradise except the number of this crow among these crows.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim and they did not expel him.”"
"8783","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us something from the origin of his book, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Wael bin Mahanat al-Taymi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O women, give in charity, even if it is your jewellery, for you will be the majority of the people of Hell.” A woman who was not from Aliyah said: Women: Why, O Messenger of God, are we the majority of the people of Hell? He said: “Because you curse a lot and are ungrateful to your spouse, and I have not seen any woman who is deficient in reason and religion more able to reach the heart of a man than you.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Jarir narrated it, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-A’mash, with additional words in it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8783 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8784","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja`far ibn Hamdan al-Zahid told us from the origin of his book, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muawiya told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith bin Al-Mustaliq, on the authority of the nephew of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, on the authority of Zainab May God be pleased with her. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed us and said: “O women, give in charity, even if it is from your jewelry, for you will have more.” The people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection.” She said: “Abdullah was a man with a light hand, so I said to him: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Does it suffice for my charity to support my husband and orphans in my care? I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was feared, so Abdullah said to me: Go and ask him. She said: So I set off and finished. To the door, a woman from the Ansar was at it. Her need was the same as mine. She said: Then Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Is charity sufficient for us to support our wives and orphans in our custody? I said: Then Bilal entered and said: At the door is Zainab. He said: “Which is the Zainab?” He said: Zainab is the wife of Abdullah and Zainab is a woman from the Ansar. They ask you to provide for their wives and orphans in their care. Does that suffice for their charity? She said: Then Bilal came out to us and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They will have two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context, and Muslim, may God have mercy on him, was the only one to narrate it briefly.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8784 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8785","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz Al-Tanukhi narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Sawda, who said: “Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, was on the wall of a house The Eastern Sanctuary was crying. Some of them said: What makes you cry, Abu Al-Walid? He said: “From here, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that he saw Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8785 - True"
"8786","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj, On the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Water like murky oil, like turbid oil. “He was brought close to it, and the scalp of his face fell into it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8786 - True"
"8787","Ibrahim bin Asmat Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Abu Rashid Al-Habrani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shibl, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The The immoral people are the people of Hell. They said: O Messenger of God, and what are the immoral people? He said: “Women.” A man said: O Messenger of God, are they not our mothers, sisters, and wives? He said: “Yes, but when they are given they are not grateful, and when they are tested they are not patient.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8787 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8788","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab informed us, about Hamdan, Hilal ibn al-Ala al-Ruqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Tufayl bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: While we are with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said the salaam during the noon prayer and the people were in the rows behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, eating something. He was eating it, but he was late, and the people were delayed, then he was late for the second time, and the people were delayed, so I said: O Messenger of God, we saw you doing something today that you were not. You do it during prayer, and he said: “Indeed, Paradise was offered to me, including its flowers and freshness, so I ate a bunch of its grapes, and if I had taken them He would eat from it from between the heaven and the earth, and they would not diminish it. So there was a barrier between me and it, and the Fire was presented to me, but when I found its burning, I retarded it. And most of the women I saw therein, if they were entrusted they were generous, and if they were asked they were generous, and when they were asked they were miserly, and when they were given they were not grateful. And I saw Amr ibn Luhay therein dragging his reed through the fire, and the most similar to the one I saw was Ma’bad ibn Aktham Al-Khuza’i.” Then Ma’bad said: O Messenger of God. By God, do you fear someone like him for me, since he is my father? He said: “No, you are a believer, but he is an unbeliever. He was the first to incite the Arabs to worship idols.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8788 - True"
"8789","Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Wazir told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, about Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Fire was presented to me and I saw in it Amr ibn Luhay Ibn Qam'ah Ibn Khandaf Abu Amr dragging his reed through the fire, and he was the first to leave the loose things and change the covenant of Abraham, peace be upon him. The most similar person I saw was Aktham bin Abi Al-Jun.” He said: Then Aktham said: O Messenger of God, does his resemblance harm me? He said: “No, you are a Muslim and he is an unbeliever.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8789 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8790","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, The one who disbelieves in his deeds and denies and disputes. It will be said to him: Your neighbors bear witness against you. He will say: They lied. It will be said: Your family and your clan. He will say: They lied, so it will be said: Swear, so they swear, then God will silence them, and their tongues will bear witness against them, and He will admit them to the Fire. “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8790 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8791","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, they said: Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, narrated to us Salam bin Miskin, said: Abu Burdah narrated, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people of Hell They will weep so much that if ships were to sink, they would sink with their tears. Indeed, they will weep for blood, meaning in place of the tears. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8791 - True"
"8792","Professor Abu Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him, told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, Abu Qutaybah told us, Farqad bin Al-Hajjaj Abu Nasr told us Uqba bin Abi Al-Hasna, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If seven caliphs were taken with their fats, and they were thrown from the brink of Hell, they would not have reached the end of it for seventy years.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8792 - Its chain of transmission is valid"
"8793","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad Al-Taymi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Hamzah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I came With Buraq, I rode behind Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he walked with us. When he rose, his legs rose, and when he descended, his hands rose. He said: So he walked. We were walking through a land of turbid clouds until we led to a good, lively land. Then I said: O Gabriel, we were walking in a land of turbid clouds. Then We were led to a bright and good land. He said: This is the land of Hell and this is the land of Paradise. He said: Then I came upon a man standing and praying, and he said: Who is this? With you, Gabriel? He said: This is your brother Muhammad. He welcomed me and prayed for blessings for me, and said: Ask for ease for your nation. I said: Who is this, O? Gabriel? He said: This is your brother Jesus, son of Mary, peace and blessings be upon him. He said: We walked, and I heard a voice and grumbling, and we came upon a man, and he said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is your brother Muhammad. He welcomed me and prayed for blessings for me, and said: Ask for ease for your nation. So I said: Who is this, O Gabriel? Gabriel? He said: This is your brother Moses. I said: Against whom was his complaining and his voice? He said: Against his Lord. He said: Yes, he knew That is from its intensity. He said: Then we walked and saw lamps for ablution. He said: I said: What is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is the tree of your father Abraham? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Do you come close to it? I said: Yes, so we approached and he welcomed me and prayed for blessings for me. Then we proceeded until we came to the Holy House, so I approached. The animal with the ring with which the prophets are tied. Then I entered the mosque, and the prophets were revealed to me, whom God Almighty and Majestic have named among them and those He was not named, so I led in prayer with them except these three people, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, may the blessings and peace of God be upon them. “This is a hadith that was unique to Abu Hamzah.” Maymoon Al-A'war, and the opinions of our imams differed about him, and he brought additions that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not mention in a narration. The ascension"
"8794","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told me, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Abu Talha Al-Rasibi told us, about Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “This nation will be gathered into three types: They will enter Paradise without being brought to account, and a group will be held accountable with an easy reckoning, and others will be passed over on their backs like upright mountains, so he asked God. about them, and He knows best, so He says: These are servants of My servants who have not associated anything with Me, and on their backs are transgressions and sins, erase them and make them upon the Jews and Christians, and enter Paradise by my mercy. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration on the condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8794 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8795","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Sinan bin Saad, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Deception And deception and betrayal in Hell.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8795 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8796","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amrawayh Al-Saffar told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Yahya bin Salamah bin Kuhail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that he used to say: I revealed Red yet? So when he saw her, he said: No, welcome, then he said: “Two of the angels, Harut and Marut, asked God Almighty to descend to earth.” So they were brought down to earth, and they were judging among the people. And when evening came, they spoke some words and ascended with them to heaven, and an appointed time was appointed for them. With a woman from the best of people, and lust was thrust upon them, so they delayed it, and lust was cast upon themselves, and they did not continue doing so until... She promised them an appointed time, so she came to them for the appointed time, and said, “Teach me the word by which you are limping.” So they taught her the word, and she spoke it, and she limped. With it, it was taken to heaven, and it was transformed, and it was made as you see. And when the evening came, they spoke the word by which they were ascending to heaven, but they did not ascend. So he was sent to them: If you wish, then the punishment of the Hereafter, and if you wish, then the punishment of this world, until the Hour comes when you will meet God Almighty. He willed to punish you both, and if He wished to have mercy on you, then one of them looked at his friend, and one of them said to his friend: Rather, we choose the punishment of this world, a thousand thousand times. Weakness, so they will be tortured until the Hour comes.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it and left the hadith of Yahya bin Salamah, on the authority of his father. Among the impossibilities that the mind rejects, there is no dispute that he is one of the craftsmen, so it is not objectionable to his father to single him out for hadiths that are unique to him. About him\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8796 - Al-Nasa’i said it is abandoned"
"8797","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Muhammad bin Issa Al-Tarsusi told us, Abu Asim told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Ja`far, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: I sat with Ibn Umar and Abu Sa`id, and one of them said to his friend: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned “the amount of sweat from the son of Adam,” and one of them said: “to the lobes of his ears,” and the other said: “the sweat is overwhelming him.” Ibn Umar pointed and wrote Between his earlobe with his index finger. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8797 - True"
"8798","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram Al-Bazzaz told us, Abu Ali Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah told us Al-Majid Al-Hanafi, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’ told us, my father told me, he said: We returned with the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted a sick man, and I placed my hand on him and said: By God, I have never seen a man more free than him today. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of something more severe than this on the Day of Resurrection, these two men riding, standing together?” to two men at that time from among his companions. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8798 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8799","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Sinan bin Saad Al-Kindi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God God Almighty, if He intends good for a servant, will hasten his punishment in this world, and if He intends evil for a servant, He will hold him accountable for his sin until he fulfills it on the Day of Resurrection. Resurrection »\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8799 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8800","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu Musa Sahl ibn Kathir told us, Ismail ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ata Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman Al-Sulami, who said: We descended from Al-Mada'in a farsang away, and when Friday came, he came, and I attended with him, so we engaged. Hudhayfah, and he said: “Indeed, God Almighty says: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has been split open} [Al-Qamar: 1] Indeed, the Hour has drawn near, and indeed the moon has He split. Indeed, the world has heralded separation. Indeed, today is the track and tomorrow is the race.’ So I said to my father: Will the people race ahead of tomorrow? He said: O my son, you are ignorant. What he means is the work today and the reward tomorrow. When the next Friday came, Hudhayfah attended and addressed us. He said: “Indeed, God Almighty says: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has been split open} [Al-Qamar: 1] Indeed, the world has heralded parting. Indeed, today The track, and tomorrow the race. Indeed, the ultimate goal is Hell, and the one who races ahead to Paradise is the one who races to Paradise. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8800 - True"
"8801","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj, On the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The dirt eats up everything from Man is nothing but the wonder of his sin. It was said: What is it, O Messenger of God? He said: “Like a mustard seed from it they grow.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8801 - True"
"8802","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Imam, may God be pleased with him, informed me. Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Affan bin Muslim, Hammam bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, who said: A group of reciters entered Abu Dharr’s house and he had a woman. She was black and had a quilted cloak over her. There were no objects or creatures over her. Abu Dharr said: Do you know what this woman is saying? You are ordering me to come. Iraq, and if I had come to Iraq, they would have said: This is the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they turned away from us from this world, and my friend is Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, made a covenant with me that the bridge to Hell is a disgrace, and in our burdens there are corruptions that we may escape from. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, if Abu Qilaba heard from Abu Dhar al-Ghaffari, may God be pleased with him.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8802 - According to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, if Abu Qilabah heard from Abu Dharr"
"8803","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Taffawi told us, Ayoub narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, that a man asked Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, about the Almighty’s saying: {And indeed, a day With your Lord is like a thousand years of what you count.} [Al-Hajj: 47] Then he said: “Who are you?” It was mentioned to him that he was a man from such-and-such, and Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “What is a day whose duration is fifty thousand years?” The man said: May God have mercy on you. I only asked you to inform us. Ibn Abbas said: “Two days that God Almighty mentioned in His Book. God knows best.” Because of them he thought to speak about the Book of God without knowledge.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8803 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
